        "id": 6043,
        "name": "Teloric",
        "username": "Teloric",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/e36b37/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-07-04T15:11:29.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Played against Citizen Dawn the other day.  Revealed the following during setup:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Citizen Truth</li>\n<li>Citizen Dare</li>\n<li>Citizen Tears</li>\n</ol>\n<p>So what do I do?  Citizen Dare does not count as a Citizen during the startup reveal.  However, Citizen Truth says, “When Citizen Dare is put into play, this card deals the hero target with the highest HP 3 melee damage; destroy this card.”</p>\n<p>So, we gave 3 damage to the hero with highest HP, and then destroyed Citizen Truth.  Then, since Citizen Dare doesn’t count, we revealed 1 more Citizen to get 3 revealed ones (Truth counts as the first revealed, Tears as the second, then another one… Hammer I think).</p>\n<p>Did we do this right?  I can’t seem to find any mention of this happening, and wasn’t sure about effects happening at the start of the game, since Citizen Truth’s card effects occur when Citizen Dare is put into play…</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:52.040Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 3,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
